#### 8. Exception Handling
**Academic name:** Exception Handling  
**Affected:** `ProcessOrder_EmptyOrder_ThrowsValidationError` (line 105)  
**Risk:** Manual try/catch is verbose and error-prone — forgetting `Assert.Fail` would make the test silently pass.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — manual try/catch
try
{
    processor.ProcessOrder(order);
    Assert.Fail("Expected an exception but none was thrown");
}
catch (ValidationException ex)
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Order must contain at least one item", ex.Message);
}
```

**Fix:** Use MSTest's built-in `Assert.ThrowsException<T>`:

```csharp
var ex = Assert.ThrowsException<ValidationException>(
    () => processor.ProcessOrder(order));
Assert.AreEqual("Order must contain at least one item", ex.Message);
```

